A Banach space $X$ is said to have the uniform approximation property (UAP) if there exist a constant $K \geq 1$ and a function $f : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ such that for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and every $n$-dimensional subspace $E \subseteq X$ there is a bounded linear operator $T : X \to X$ satisfying:
(i) $T|_E = \mathrm{id}_E$;
(ii) $\|T\| \leq K$;
(iii) $\operatorname{rank}(T) \leq f(n)$.

Question: If a Banach space $X$ has the uniform approximation property, must its dual space $X^*$ also have the uniform approximation property?

